### commit
be377f86 fix(weather): callers that waited through a failure are handed it, however long it took

With the backoff counted from the start of the failed run, a run that
outlasts its own backoff -- a 60 s timeout, and Pirate Weather tries three
times -- ends with its pause already over, and every caller that had been
waiting on the lock meanwhile went to the network in turn. A caller now
notes when it arrived, before taking the lock; one that arrived before the
latest failure ended waited through it and is handed its outcome like the
others, whether or not the pause has run out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

